analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/full_runs/gpt_oss_120b_review_pipeline_all4027_current_rep2_watchdog_20260511T1642Z/job_11575/guideline_pilot_raw_completed.csv:4736:2799,Chrysalis: decoding tissue compartments in spatial transcriptomics with archetypal analysis,chrysalis decoding tissue compartments in spatial transcriptomics with archetypal analysis,10.1101/2023.08.17.553606,,,,"Dissecting tissue compartments in spatial transcriptomics (ST) remains challenging due to limited spatial resolution and dependence on single-cell reference data. We present Chrysalis, a novel method to rapidly detect tissue compartments through spatially variable gene (SVG) detection and archetypal analysis without external references. We applied Chrysalis on ST datasets originating from various species, tissues and technologies and demonstrated state-of-the-art performance in identifying cellular niches.","Túrós D, Vasiljevic J, Hahn K, Rottenberg S, Valdeolivas A.",2023.0,,2023-08-18,,['biorxiv_medrxiv'],1,['10.1101/2023.08.17.553606'],1,,,,,2627,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""no"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""none"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes a novel method for detecting tissue compartments in spatial transcriptomics using gene detection and archetypal analysis, with no mention of natural-language text, prompts, or text‑bio mapping.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,no,no,none,none,none,none,not_assessed,none,"The abstract describes a novel method for detecting tissue compartments in spatial transcriptomics using gene detection and archetypal analysis, with no mention of natural-language text, prompts, or text‑bio mapping.","{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""no"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""EC3_not_generative"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract presents Chrysalis, an archetypal‑analysis method for decoding tissue compartments, with no generative architecture or decoder described, and no evidence of a foundation‑model pretraining regime.""}",primary_model_paper,no,no,EC3_not_generative,none,not_assessed,not_assessed,none,clear_exclude,"The abstract presents Chrysalis, an archetypal‑analysis method for decoding tissue compartments, with no generative architecture or decoder described, and no evidence of a foundation‑model pretraining regime.",EXCLUDE,EXCLUDE,False,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
