data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/adjudication/shard_07/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003517_bdcbcbd932f3/prompt.txt:719:Each training sample is a tuple ( X ctrl , X target , T , M pert , p ) where X ctrl , X target ∈ R S × G ′ are control and perturbed expression matrices over S cells and G ′ subsampled genes, T ∈ Z S × G ′ contains gene vocabulary indices, M pert ∈ { 0 , 1 } S × G ′ is a binary perturbation mask indicating which gene positions contain revealed perturbed signal, and p identifies the perturbation. The batch is reshaped from ( B,S,G ′ ) to ( B · S, G ′ ) for token-level processing.
